t even after years of abuse and  multiple attempts to kill each other  Halle is still obsessed with a Joker  shortly after arriving at Ivy's new pad  Harley and sis she's over mr. J then  seconds later excitedly asked if he's  called by the end of the issue the three  women have agreed to join forces and  leave Riddler's apartment for an  abandoned animal shelter Gotham City  sirens would only last 26 issues but if  nothing else it marked an important step  in the evolution of Harley Quinn  after all this series saw Harley's first  comic team up with other women in lead  roles a pattern that would be repeated  throughout the characters history in  August 2009 both DC fans and gamers  alike were treated to one of the  franchise's best ever video game  Batman Arkham Asylum in this hit game  the player takes on the role of Batman  who after delivering Joker to the  titular asylum is forced to suffer  breakout conceived by the Clown Prince  of Crime himself naturally Harley is all  too happy to get involved Holi appears a  fair bit throughout the game though  she's one of the only BAP villains that  the player never confronts physically  after sending squads of thugs after the  hero Harley is easily overpowered by  Batman in a cutscene was perhaps most  significant about Harley's spot in the  game however is that it's her first  major appearance in media without a  classic Jester suit instead she was a  nurse outfit sporting the twin ponytails  that would later become a Harley Quinn  staple believe it or not Harley Quinn  didn't appear at all in the first three  volumes of Suicide Squad but in the year  since she's since become such an  inseparable part of task force eggs that  is difficult to imagine there was a time  when the team of villains could function  without her Harley's 2011 debut in  Suicide Squad came as part of DC's line  wide reboot that new 52 during which  Harley's jester Luke was abandoned for  colourful ponytails and a much skimpier  outfit Adam glass